142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 106 0 R
/T (This project builds a predictive analytics system that stratifies anonymized patient populations into risk groups using clinical, demographic, utilization, and longitudinal health features. Several supervised learning algorithms are compared, with explainability methods used to identify influential variables. The platform presents risk probabilities and cohort-level analytics rather than autonomous clinical decisions. Evaluation covers discrimination, calibration, subgroup performance, and appropriate handling of missing and imbalanced data.)
/E (This project builds a predictive analytics system that stratifies anonymized patient populations into risk groups using clinical, demographic, utilization, and longitudinal health features. Several supervised learning algorithms are compared, with explainability methods used to identify influential variables. The platform presents risk probabilities and cohort-level analytics rather than autonomous clinical decisions. Evaluation covers discrimination, calibration, subgroup performance, and appropriate handling of missing and imbalanced data.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
